                      <TH>Roast Pig Oyster Dressing</TH></TR>
                    <TR>
                      <TD>1 large onion</TD></TR>
                    <TR>
                      <TD>1 quart oysters, chopped, with =
liquid</TD></TR>
                    <TR>
                      <TD>1 pound butter, melted</TD></TR>
                    <TR>
                      <TD>8 quarts toasted bread cubes</TD></TR>
                    <TR>
                      <TD>3 eggs, lightly beaten</TD></TR>
                    <TR>
                      <TD>5 stalks celery, diced</TD></TR>
                    <TR>
                      <TD>salt and pepper</TD></TR>
                    <TR>
                      <TD>2 cups milk</TD></TR>
                    <TR>
                      <TD><BR>Cook onions and oysters with liquid in =
butter=20
                        until oysters start to curl; cool. Add bread =
cubes,=20
                        eggs, celery and milk, tossing lightly. Add salt =
and=20
                        pepper to taste. Bake extra dressing in =
casserole dish=20
                        at 350 degrees F for 45 minutes. Note: The liver =
and=20
                        heart may be steamed, diced and added to a light =
brown=20
                        gravy to be served with the dressing.=20
                  </TD></TR></TBODY></TABLE><PRE>
</PRE>
