                    <TR>
                      <TH>Brunswick Stew</TH></TR>
                    <TR>
                      <TD>Brunswick stew is a traditional dish served at =

                        Southern barbecues. It is a favorite because of =
the=20
                        flavor combination of chicken, beef and pork. =
The dish=20
                        is long on flavor and short on leftovers.
                        <P></P></TD></TR>
                    <TR>
                      <TD>1 hen (6 pounds) chicken</TD></TR>
                    <TR>
                      <TD>1 Boston Butt (6 pounds) lean pork</TD></TR>
                    <TR>
                      <TD>1 roast (6 pounds) beef chuck</TD></TR>
                    <TR>
                      <TD>15 cups (120 ounces) canned tomatoes</TD></TR>
                    <TR>
                      <TD>1 cup (8 ounces) tomato paste</TD></TR>
                    <TR>
                      <TD>4 cups (32 ounces) cream style corn</TD></TR>
                    <TR>
                      <TD>2 cups (16 ounces) whole kernel corn</TD></TR>
                    <TR>
                      <TD>4 cups (2) large onions, diced</TD></TR>
                    <TR>
                      <TD>1 ounce Worcestershire sauce</TD></TR>
                    <TR>
                      <TD>1 Tbsp. (1/2 ounce) butter</TD></TR>
                    <TR>
                      <TD>8 Tbsp. (4 ounces) salt</TD></TR>
                    <TR>
                      <TD>4 Tbsp. (1 ounce) black pepper</TD></TR>
                    <TR>
                      <TD>4 Tbsp. (2 ounces) vinegar or lemon =
juice</TD></TR>
                    <TR>
                      <TD><BR>Place meat in a large kettle, add a small =
amount=20
                        of water and cook until meat comes off the bone =
easily.=20
                        Remove meat and de-bone. Strain broth through a =
cloth=20
                        and return it to the kettle. Grind meat through =
a=20
                        1/4-inch plate or chop into small pieces by =
hand. Add=20
                        meat, tomatoes, corn and other ingredients. Cook =
on low=20
                        heat for 45 minutes, stirring frequently to =
prevent=20
                        sticking. Cool, then package in freezer =
containers and=20
                        freeze. To retain a comparable flavor, do not =
reduce=20
                        this recipe by more than one =
half.</TD></TR></TBODY></TABLE><PRE>
</PRE>
